# if — the branch the condition picks, and only that one.
#
# `if << $env … << $cond condition << $t (…) << $f (…)` is if/else. Its two
# branches are function-typed slots, so the call stands where it is and is not
# run there: each one goes to the switch that is taken, and that switch runs it
# in a child environment of its own. The switch that is not taken answers
# `never`, and the sum drops it (`never | a = a`), so what is left is the branch
# the condition picked — and only that branch's call was ever run. That is
# why this is the sum of the two switches and not a call to one of them: the sum
# is what decides which branch survives.
#
# The two switches are builtin operators (`builtin.echo_or_never`,
# `builtin.never_or_echo`, viba/builtin.viba), so this file needs no import, and
# neither do the modules that call it.
#
# A branch is the call it stands for, still owing its environment: a step of
# another file (`counters.tick`), a call that has not been given one yet, or a
# value already worked out, handed out with `builtin.echo`. A branch that gives
# its environment itself is a call that runs right there, so that side runs
# whatever the condition says.
#
# Several steps — or a value that must not be computed yet — are a `sequential`
# chain. This language has no `block` and no `lambda: value`; `sequential` does
# both jobs: its steps are calls that still owe their environment, so the block
# runs when, and only when, the switch hands it one.
#
#     block =
#         sequential
#       << $n (counters.add_to << $x 40)
#       << (builtin.echo << $x ($var "n"))
#
# The environment is a parameter: giving it is what runs this call, and every
# module call gets a sub-environment of its own
# (`args.env.sub_env << args.env << "if"`), so two if/else at one place answer
# two different layers. The two switches are given this call's own environment,
# and the branch they run is a child of it.

__decl__ =
    Any
  <- $env Env
  <- $cond bool
  <- $t (Any <- $env Env)
  <- $f (Any <- $env Env)

args = __get_args__ << __decl__

__impl__ =
    Oneof
  | (echo_or_never << $env args.env << $cond args.cond << $get_v args.t)
  | (never_or_echo << $env args.env << $cond args.cond << $get_v args.f)
